COMPONENTS OF NETWORK: 
To build a simple network we need, 
     1. End Devices ( Computers, laptop, mobiles, server, cloud servers ) 
     2. NIC - Network Interface Card
     3. Transmission Media ( Wired or wireless) 
     4. Intermidate Devices ( Router, Switc, Firewall, Access point, Modem ) 
     5. IP Addressing 
     6. Networking Protocols 

|S.No	    |Component	                        |Description	                             |   Example	                           |            Why It Is Needed
|-------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
|1	         |End Devices	                   | Devices that send/receive data	         |   Laptop, Desktop, Server, Printer	  |     At least 2 devices are required to form a network |
|2	         |Network Interface Card (NIC)	    | Hardware that connects device to network   |  Ethernet port, WiFi adapter	            |     Provides MAC address and enables communication    | 
|3	         |Transmission Media	              | Medium through which data travels	         |   Ethernet cable, Fiber optic, WiFi	  |     Carries data between devices                      |
|4	         |Switch	                        | Connects devices within same network	    |   8-port switch	                      |     Enables internal communication in LAN             |
|5	         |Router	                        | Connects different networks	              |  Home WiFi router	                      |     Connects LAN to Internet                          |
|6	         Modem	                             | Connects network to ISP	                   |   Broadband modem	                      |     Converts ISP signal for router                    |
|7	         |IP Addressing	                   | Logical addressing system	              |  192.168.1.10	                           |     Identifies devices uniquely                       |
|8	         |Network Protocols	              | Rules for communication	                   |   TCP/IP, HTTP, DNS	                 |     Ensures proper data transfer                      |

Intermediate Devices: 
1. SWITCH: - A switch connects multiple devices inside the same network (LAN).
             Example: All computers inside your office connected to one switch.
             Technical Explanation - A switch is a Layer 2 networking device used to connect multiple devices within the same local area network. 
                                     It forwards data based on MAC addresses and reduces unnecessary traffic by sending data only to the intended device.

2. ROUTER: - A router connects different networks together.
             Example: Your home network ↔ Internet.
             Technical Explanation - A router works at Layer 3 (Network Layer) and uses IP addresses to forward packets between networks.
                                     A router is a Layer 3 device that connects different networks and forwards packets based on IP addresses. 
                                     It enables communication between internal networks and external networks such as the internet.

3. FIREWALL: - A firewall protects the network by blocking unauthorized traffic.
               In Cloud: AWS Security Group = Virtual Firewall & Network ACL = Network-level firewall
               Technical Explanation - A firewall monitors and filters incoming and outgoing traffic based on predefined security rules.
                                       A firewall is a network security device that monitors and controls incoming and outgoing traffic based on security rules. 
                                       It protects the network from unauthorized access and cyber threats.

4. MODEM - A modem connects your network to the ISP.
           Technical Explanation - Modem stands for Modulator-Demodulator. It converts digital signals from your computer into analog signals for transmission and vice versa.
                                   A modem is a device that connects a local network to an Internet Service Provider by converting digital data into signals suitable for transmission and vice versa.
